The '''fourth series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' began airing on 20 August 2013.<ref name="digital">{{cite news |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s215/great-british-bake-off/news/a505011/great-british-bake-off-returns-first-look-at-series-four-watch.html |title= 'Great British Bake Off' returns: First look at series four – Watch |work=Digital Spy |date=8 August 2013  |author= Alex Fletcher }}</ref> [[Mel Giedroyc]] and [[Sue Perkins]] again presented the show and [[Mary Berry (food writer)|Mary Berry]] and [[Paul Hollywood]] returned as judges.<ref name="guardian">{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2013/jul/20/bake-off-behind-the-scenes |title=Behind the scenes at The Great British Bake Off |author=Louise Carpenter |work=The Observer |date=20 July 2013 }}</ref> As with [[The Great British Bake Off (Series 3)|series three]], the competition was held at [[Harptree Court]] in [[East Harptree]], [[Somerset]].<ref name="somerset">{{cite web |url=http://www.thisissomerset.co.uk/Great-British-Bake-returns-screen-East-Harptree/story-19639200-detail/story.html |title=Great British Bake Off returns to the screen – and to East Harptree |author=Ben O'Brien |work=The Somerset Standard and Guardian |date=9 August 2013 }}</ref>

13,000 amateur bakers applied to appear on the programme, and 100 were selected for screen test, with the best 60 advancing to a three-day audition.<ref name="guardian"/> From these, 13 contestants were chosen this year so the judges could eliminate two people whenever they wanted.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.express.co.uk/news/showbiz/420639/FIRST-LOOK-Great-British-Bake-off-is-back |title=FIRST LOOK: Great British Bake off is back! |author=Kelby McNally |date= 8 August 2013 |work=The Daily Express }}</ref>

The winner of the ''Great British Bake Off'' 2013 was [[Frances Quinn]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2013/oct/22/frances-quinn-wins-great-british-bake-off |title=Frances Quinn wins The Great British Bake Off |first=John|last= Plunkett|date= 22 October 2013 |work=The Guardian }}</ref>

The fourth series was broadcast as the second season on [[PBS]] in the United States.

