=== Episode 9: French week (Semi-final) ===
This week's theme was all things [[French cuisine|French]].<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b03dyxp9 |title=French Week |work=BBC}}</ref> In the signature challenge, the bakers are challenged to make 3 different types of savoury canapés; [[choux pastry]], [[Shortcrust pastry|shortcrust]] or [[Puff pastry|rough puff]] pastry, and a third pastry of their choice, to be done in {{frac|2|1|2}} hours. For the technical bake, the bakers are challenged to make a [[Charlotte (cake)|Charlotte Royale]] consisting of Swiss roll surrounding a [[Bavarian cream|bavarois]] in {{frac|2|1|2}} hours. It is set with gelatin to form a firm dome when turned out. In the showstopper challenge, the bakers are challenged to bake an iconic French patisserie, the [[opera cake]], in {{frac|2|1|2}} hours.

